      "sha": "02a9f266c0568184613e4d721afb534cc4988a5c",
      "message": "feat(core): add runtime plugin management (hot add/remove)\n\nRoadmap #11 (plugin hot-reload) is blocked on #9 (widget API\nstandardization), but a large, useful subset is achievable today: plugins\nwhose hooks are all hot-pluggable (cmExtensions, shortcuts) can be\ninstalled onto and removed from a *live* editor via a new Compartment-backed\nregistry, with no recreation — document, undo history, selection, and\nscroll are all preserved. Plugins declaring construction-time hooks\n(widgets, remarkPlugins, slashCommands, commands, handlers) are rejected\nwith an explicit, actionable error rather than silently half-installed.\n\n- core: `addPlugin` / `removePlugin` / `getPlugins` + `pluginsChange` event\n  on EditorAPI, backed by a hook classifier + Compartment reconfigure\n  (packages/core/src/runtime-plugins.ts)\n- new package `@floatboat/nexus-plugin-typewriter`: typewriter-mode cursor\n  centering, used as an end-to-end proof of the mechanism (hot-pluggable\n  by construction). Getting its scrolling correct surfaced a real\n  CodeMirror pitfall — see design.md D4 for the investigation — CM keeps a\n  single pending scroll-target slot that native \"nearest\" input scrolling\n  overwrites every keystroke, racing any `scrollIntoView` effect. Fixed by\n  reading/writing scrollTop directly via requestMeasure instead.\n- electron-demo: a Plugins panel (mechanism/policy split — core knows\n  nothing about panels; the demo decides what to install and when) with a\n  dynamic-import install/uninstall toggle for the typewriter plugin\n- docs: core README runtime-plugin section + hook classification table,\n  ROADMAP entries (en/zh)\n\nFull OpenSpec proposal, design rationale, and spec deltas in\nopenspec/changes/add-runtime-plugin-management/. 543 tests passing.\n\nAI-assisted implementation (Claude Code), per CONTRIBUTING.md disclosure\nrequirements — see PR description for scope of assistance.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "date": "2026-07-03T01:09:05Z"
    }
  ],
